    "explanation": "To both parties — this resolves the dispute over trip TRP-00520.\n\nWhat the record shows. The in-app chat (EV-CHAT-00520) records the rider asking at 11:37:10 — thirty seconds after the trip started at 11:36:40 — 'can stop at Sheng Siong Blk 501 first? need to grab something', with the platform's resolved waypoint for Sheng Siong Supermarket Blk 501 Tampines Central 1, and the driver replying 'ok' at 11:37:30. The rider confirms the request in her own statement: 'I did ask him to stop at the supermarket, that is true.'\n\nThe deviation. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00520) records 5.63 km — trace_distance_km, which governs over the trip record's rounded 5.6 km actual_distance_km — against the booked optimal of 3.1 km, an excess of 2.53 km or 81.6%, which would pass both POL-RD-01 gates and be MATERIAL. But that extra distance was requested by the rider, so POL-RD-04 excludes it: no deviation is established and no distance refund arises for the rider under POL-RD-02. Her position that the fare 'should have been the same as always' does not by itself create a refund, because the detour was hers to request. Her point that the 200 m waypoint corroboration could not be run is noted but not decisive: the clause's own unavailability test (a null waypoint_hint) is not met, and the detour is confirmed by her own admission and the trace's extra distance and stationary/slow-speed stretch.\n\nThe unbilled distance. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00520) billed the rider for only 3.1 km of distance while the trace records 5.63 km. 5.63 − 3.1 = 2.53 km was driven and never billed. That exceeds the 1.0 km threshold in POL-RD-04's compensation limb, so the driver is owed SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre: 2.53 × 0.75 = SGD 1.8975, rounded up to SGD 1.90, well inside the SGD 15.00 per-trip cap. The 2.4 km figure in the driver's narrative is not used; the record supports 2.53 km.\n\nOther points. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes (121 fixes, 10 s cadence, max_gap_sec 0.0), so POL-RD-07 does not displace the trace-based finding and no independent corroboration is required. No repeat-deviation pattern arises (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across 250 completed trips), so no POL-RD-06 conduct referral is made. There are no ERP, toll or surcharge lines, so POL-RD-09 yields no correction. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00520-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT): it carries no fact and only means no road-closure exoneration is available. Profile fields such as rating, lifetime trips, acceptance rate and active region are context only under POL-GEN-01 and ground no finding either way.\n\nConfidence. The deciding unbilled-distance figure is carried by the GPS trace and the fare breakdown, both at weight 1.0, so no weight cap presses confidence below 0.85. The money the ruling moves is SGD 1.90, paid to the driver; both amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd carry that same figure and no second payment or rider refund is created."
